","header_size":"h3","title_color":"#161616CC","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"30","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"3c22650","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"“What should be our subscription strategy?” is a question we are often asked, in the journey of our partnership with SaaS companies for crafting and engineering their product experience.
