","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":34,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":34,"sizes":[]},"title_color":"#333333"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"f77cf44","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Imagine you’ve just joined a fast-growing company that’s scaling rapidly across multiple products. Each team works independently, building components and UI elements as they go. It works well—at first. But soon, the cracks start to show: inconsistent designs, duplicated components, and codebases that don’t quite align.
<br> <br>
As the developer tasked with fixing this, you realize that what your organization needs is a design system. A system that ensures everyone is on the same page, no matter how many teams or products there are.

","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"f67371d","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Understanding Inconsistencies: The Birth of a Unified Design System
","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":34,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":48,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":36,"sizes":[]},"title_color":"#333333"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"67ebeea","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"The first step is understanding the scope of the problem. You sit down with your team and realize that every team has their version of the same button, card, or modal. Worse yet, the designs are slightly different. What you need is a single source of 
<br> <br>
truth—a design system that unifies these scattered elements and ensures consistency.

","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"99b031e","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<b>A design system is more than just components. It’s a shared language that bridges the gap between designers and developers.</b>","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"652ee76","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Collaboration is Key: Designers and Developers Working Together
","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":34,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":48,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":36,"sizes":[]},"title_color":"#333333"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"46fea7d","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Before getting into the details of design tokens, it’s important to highlight what makes a design system successful: collaboration. Designers and developers bring their unique skills and perspectives, and when they work together, they can create a seamless user experience. By aligning their efforts, they ensure that designs turn into functional, reusable components that work smoothly in the final product.

","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"78e6e9d","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"‍Design Tokens as the Building Blocks of Consistency‍
","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"75f6b89","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"You can’t build this system alone. You pull in the design team, and they provide you with everything you need: a Figma file with components, color schemes, typography, and spacing. You look at the designs and see that every component and design token has been carefully planned.
<br> <br>
But translating those designs into reusable code requires collaboration. You work with designers to ensure that the handoff is smooth and that the design tokens—colors, fonts, and spacing—are consistent across all components.

‍","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"9abd71c","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"‍Managing Design Tokens Across Projects ","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"066fafe","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"For single projects, a basic CSS or JSON file may suffice. For multiple projects, a single source of truth becomes essential. The Design Tokens Format Module W3C Community Draft offers a standardized format for defining tokens, promoting consistency and collaboration. The draft provides an excellent breakdown of tokens, helping teams understand how to structure and think about them effectively for scalable design systems.

