","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":34,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":48,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":36,"sizes":[]},"title_color":"#333333"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"2c0d2fe","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>As you start thinking about how to build this system, you weigh your options. Should you create everything from scratch, defining each component from the ground up, or could you leverage a pre-built library? For example, if you’re using React, you might consider a library like MUI. This approach allows you to customize components to fit your design system while benefiting from the time-saving features of a pre-built library.<br /><br /><br />A general principle is to strike a balance between efficiency and flexibility. Combining a pre-built library with tailored customizations ensures time-saving benefits while maintaining consistency and aligning with your brand’s identity.</p>","text_color":"#464646","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Brockmann Regular","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"300","typography_line_height":{"unit":"px","size":31,"sizes":[]},"_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false},"_padding_tablet":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"_padding_mobile":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"a0f3923","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"Choosing the Right Library
